---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "17 July 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="BAGGAGE — Privacy Policy"
  description="How BAGGAGE handles your data. Short version: your packing lists stay in your browser, and there are no accounts."
>
  <Header />
  <main>
    <section class="policySection">
      <div class="container">
        <article class="policy">
          <span class="eyebrow">BAGGAGE</span>
          <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
          <p class="updated">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

          <p>
            <a href="https://baggage.hayley.codes/">BAGGAGE</a> is a little web app for
            organising the things you pack and carry. This policy explains what it does
            with your data. The short version: almost nothing.
          </p>

          <h2>Your lists stay on your device</h2>
          <p>
            Everything you create in BAGGAGE — your trips, lists, and items — is stored
            locally in your browser (using your browser's local storage). It never leaves
            your device and is never sent to a server. There are no accounts and no logins,
            so there's nothing for me to see, store, or share.
          </p>
          <p>
            Because your data lives in your browser, clearing your browser data or using a
            different device or browser means starting fresh. I can't recover lists for you,
            because I never have them in the first place.
          </p>

          <h2>Anonymous analytics</h2>
          <p>
            BAGGAGE uses <a href="https://vercel.com/docs/analytics">Vercel Web Analytics</a>
            to get a rough sense of how many people visit and which pages they use. This is
            privacy-friendly by design: it doesn't use cookies, doesn't track you across other
            websites, and doesn't collect information that identifies you personally. It only
            records aggregate, anonymous usage.
          </p>

          <h2>Supporting BAGGAGE (Buy Me a Coffee)</h2>
          <p>
            If you choose to support BAGGAGE with a donation, payments are handled entirely by
            <a href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/">Buy Me a Coffee</a> and their payment
            processors (such as Stripe). I never see or store your card or billing details.
          </p>
          <p>
            Depending on your Buy Me a Coffee settings, I may receive your name (or a pseudonym),
            email address, and any message you send — used only to say thank you. See the
            <a href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/privacy-policy">Buy Me a Coffee Privacy Policy</a>
            for how they handle your payment data.
          </p>

          <h2>What I don't do</h2>
          <p>
            No accounts. No advertising. No selling or sharing of data. No tracking cookies.
            I don't collect your name, email, or any personal details, because the app simply
            doesn't ask for them.
          </p>

          <h2>Children's privacy</h2>
          <p>
            BAGGAGE isn't directed at children, and it doesn't collect personal information from
            anyone — including children under 13.
          </p>

          <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
          <p>
            If BAGGAGE ever changes in a way that affects your data, I'll update this page and
            the date at the top.
          </p>

          <h2>Questions</h2>
          <p>
            If anything here is unclear, you're welcome to reach out at
            <a href="mailto:hello@hayley.codes">hello@hayley.codes</a>.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  /* BAGGAGE theme — pink accent with a deep-purple pop (see ProjectSection.module.css) */
  .policySection {
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
    padding: 128px 0 96px;
    background:
      radial-gradient(1000px 520px at 15% -10%, #e8479f, transparent 55%),
      radial-gradient(760px 480px at 105% 110%, rgba(102, 23, 203, 0.3), transparent 60%),
      #cb228f;
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  @media (min-width: 720px) {
    .policySection {
      padding: 160px 0 128px;
    }
  }

  .policy {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }

  /* Chip — translucent white on the pink, like the project cards */
  .policy :global(.eyebrow) {
    color: #ffffff;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    border-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.4);
  }

  .policy h1 {
    font-family: "Caveat Brush", var(--font-family-heading);
    color: #ffffff;
  }

  .policy h2 {
    font-family: "Caveat Brush", var(--font-family-heading);
    color: #ffffff;
    margin-top: 1.6em;
  }

  .policy p {
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.92);
  }

  .updated {
    color: #ffe3f1 !important;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: -0.4em;
    margin-bottom: 2em;
  }

  /* Links — white and underlined so they stay legible on the pink */
  .policy a {
    color: #ffffff;
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-decoration-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55);
    text-underline-offset: 3px;
  }

  .policy a:hover {
    color: #ffe3f1;
    text-decoration-color: #ffe3f1;
  }
</style>
